  "uuid": "a3255f64-71c8-4de2-901c-132419222b94",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "f0678676-11a7-7b37-2a1d-9fa803bab60d",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "a2726c0c-6d9f-6704-df43-d11c9d034bb8",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The programme featured a dynamic book swap, a dedicated silent reading hour, and a social media initiative encouraging participants to share their reading experiences. The atmosphere was characterized by focused engagement and the tangible pleasure of reading, transcending the external weather conditions.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "D.E.A.R. Day",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.ala.org/aasl/advocacy/promo/dear#:~:text=Description%20%26%20History-%2cD.E.A.R.%2cfor%20author%20Beverly%20Cleary%27s%20birthday.",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", traditionally observed on April 12, commemorates the birthday of author Beverly Cleary, who advocated for dedicated reading time. The event underscores the importance of prioritizing reading, cultivating a lifelong appreciation for literature, and promoting literacy across all demographics.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In an era dominated by digital media, D.E.A.R. Day reaffirms the enduring value of reading, regardless of format. It highlights reading as a fundamental source of knowledge, inspiration, and creative thought.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"The event was truly inspiring. I had the opportunity to engage with 'The 5 Second Rule,' a book that emphasized the importance of decisive action and pursuing goals with courage,\" said Roselyne Gombe, a student from the Institute for Educational Development, East Africa (IED, EA).The AKU Tanzania Library remains committed to fostering a strong reading culture, encouraging the university community to dedicate time to reading as a catalyst for intellectual growth and innovation. Reading, in any form, serves as a foundation for future ideas and discoveries.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
